# glibc protects tzset_internal with its private tzset_lock, which distributions build without
# ThreadSanitizer instrumentation (seen on Fedora 45 and Ubuntu 26.04),
# so TSan cannot see it. Reports observed here are malloc/free of glibc's old_tz
# during concurrent libgit2 git_signature_now calls, not accesses to Holder data.
# Source: https://github.com/bminor/glibc/blob/master/time/tzset.c
# Limitation: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerCppManual#non-instrumented-code
race:tzset_internal
